WEBVTT

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.600
Kikou wa nori no warui

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.340
Watashi ga sanka suru

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:22.380
Hisabisa no doraibu de minna hai tenshon

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.250
Kare mo kuru no

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.850
Myaku ga ima wa nakutomo

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.590
Zettai ikimasu tomo

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:38.630
Sugoi sugoi pookaa faisu dato shitara

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.770
Aru yo nante

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:48.810
Umi wa hiyake suru kara, yama ni shiyou tte

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:58.390
Koo-to no kisetsu nanoni kanchigai shiteru

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:02.620
Doushite nano?

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:06.590
Konna ureshikute

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:14.400
Chigiresouna hodo waratte iru noni

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:22.940
Kare no senaka mite wa mune tsumaru

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:30.910
Taenai egao no utsu no naka de

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:36.420
What's for dinner?

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:37.490
What is it?

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:39.690
Wow, hamburger!

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:40.460
Hamburger!

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:41.000
Rose, I want the egg that goes
on my hamburger fried hard!
Hamburger!

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.230
Rose, I want the egg that goes
on my hamburger fried hard!

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:46.900
I want mine soft, Rose!

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.270
The hard one is better!

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.870
I like the soft one better!

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:52.170
And you mix it with stuff!

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.940
I don't wanna do that!
The hamburger will get all mushy!

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:58.010
That's okay, because it tastes so good that way!

00:01:58.010 --> 00:01:59.380
Isn't that right, Rose?

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:01.580
I'd never wanna do that!

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:04.920
Oh, no, Rose! The egg will get hard!

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:05.750
Yes!

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.060
Oh, I'm sorry. Do you want your
egg hard or soft?

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:10.690
Hard!

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:11.230
Soft!
Hard!

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:11.990
Soft!
All right, all right.

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:12.790
All right, all right.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:15.360
Then I should make mine over-medium!

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.600
Me too!

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.500
Hey, why did you change your mind?

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:20.340
I want mine just like Rose's!

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.960
That's not fair!

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.650
Rose, it's already past over-medium!

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.350
Oh, shoot!

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:34.080
Jeez, what do I do with you?

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.120
What do I do with you?

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.690
I'm sorry. Come on, have a seat.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.190
What do I do with you?

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:40.890
I like a hard-fried egg too anyway!

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.390
Oh, well, it's much better than
a bunch of vegetables!

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:43.890
Yes, definitely!

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:44.460
My memories...
Yes, definitely!

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:44.930
My memories...
We're not bugs!

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:45.460
Nope, we're not bugs!
We're not bugs!

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:45.690
Nope, we're not bugs!

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:46.460
Nope, we're not bugs!
If it means that I'm going to
forget about Paul and Carrie,

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.930
If it means that I'm going to
forget about Paul and Carrie,

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.970
I might as well be dead.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.370
Episode #18
Slight Hope
I might as well be dead.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:54.960
Episode #18
Slight Hope

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:58.970
So, this is what you want?

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:00.270
Yeah...

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:06.310
If she disappears, my uncle and the others
will have no choice but to take action.

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:09.610
That will give them only the right choice,
which is to fight against the Animus.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.420
Right choice, huh?

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:16.160
Looks like the medicine is working.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.130
What are you planning to do with her?

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.630
It was a mistake that Lise ever met me,

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:27.230
so I'll return her to the place of the beginning.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:32.730
Missing girls...

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:37.650
My instincts are screaming that I shouldn't
get involved in this case.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:44.280
Alarm bells are going off like
crazy in my gut, but...

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.440
Th...This is it!

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:05.740
Lise!

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:08.240
Is she a ghost?

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:17.790
What the hell is Rose doing?

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.580
She might not come.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.690
We'd better go find Rose.

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:25.760
Why?

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.260
Huh?

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.200
What?

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.190
Because it's our joint responsibility?

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.260
I just can't leave Rose alone.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:39.740
She's probably with her brother
and sister right about now.

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:41.810
Her brother and sister...

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:46.880
What's dear to Rose...What she must protect...

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:49.550
If that's the case, maybe we
should leave her alone.

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:52.650
I bet she wants to lock herself in the house.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.990
Maybe you're right.

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:56.460
Kate...

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:02.500
Who knows, Rose might not even
wish to be with us,

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:03.770
but...

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:05.230
But, what?

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:11.800
We're the only people who can understand the
sorrow she's dealing with all alone right now.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.650
I'm sure she's crying like a baby.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:19.850
I'm talking about Rose.

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:24.350
She'll be shutting all the windows,
all nervous about ignoring this call-up.

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:26.690
But Rose isn't the same Rose anymore.

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:28.120
Why don't you admit it already?

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.020
I know she's going to cry!

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:29.520
Rachel?
I know she's going to cry!

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:30.690
Rachel?

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:34.590
So, I can't leave her alone.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.500
Let's go see Rose.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.130
Yeah...

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:52.680
I wonder what's gonna happen to her?

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:56.780
It'd cause a serious panic if a dead
person came back to life.

00:05:56.780 --> 00:06:00.020
I don't think her parents will make it public.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:05.460
She's going to be confined in the house and live
the rest of her life quietly, as a dead person.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.960
And one day, she'll become a real corpse.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.370
What a horrible thing we've done to her.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.490
She's still a human, even if she's dead.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:17.060
If she can die as a human,
then she's not doing so bad.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:22.410
We don't have any more business here.
Take the car to the street.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.950
You're not even going to say goodbye to her?

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:29.250
I could, but nothing matters to her right now.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.280
Is it cold?

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:42.760
It'll come back to you little by little.

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:47.760
Different sensations and different feelings, so...

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:54.830
I'm sorry.

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:36.620
She won't answer the phone.

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:38.150
Is she at home?

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:40.660
Probably so, but...

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.990
What should we do? Should we just go
there and ring the doorbell?

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:45.790
I don't know if we should go that far.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.200
Rose!

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.330
I can't believe you'd call me on my
cellular phone this late at night!

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:52.470
What if that woke my siblings up?

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:53.330
I'm sorry, but...

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:54.000
I'm sick of it!
I'm sorry, but...

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.240
I'm sick of it!

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:58.270
I don't wanna fight anymore.

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:00.510
It won't change anything whether
we win or lose anyway.

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:02.740
If that's how it is, then I don't wanna fight.

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:06.110
Yeah, that's fine.

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:09.150
We came here because we
were worried about you.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:14.520
"Worried"? That's a lie! It's all because
we're jointly responsible for this, right?

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:15.760
That's the only reason, right?

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:18.030
We're not in the mood tonight, you know.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.060
What?

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.930
I mean, we're not planning to fight tonight.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:25.730
But...But...But...

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:31.410
Believe it already! This isn't about
a call-up or joint responsibility.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.170
Why?

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:36.540
Is it a problem if we worry about you?

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:41.120
I just don't wanna forget...

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.180
I know...

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:45.550
...about Paul and Carrie.

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:46.520
I know...

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:54.560
I don't wanna forget about my mom, my dad,
Sara and the nurses at the hospital.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:57.970
The sale at the market, how much homework
I have to turn in tomorrow,

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.770
even the smell of the freshly-dried sheets...

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:01.900
Everything, I mean, everything...

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:03.370
Rose...

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:07.280
I don't want to forget it!

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:11.140
I don't want to forget it! I'm scared.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.780
I'll be alone when I wake up, right?

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:17.390
Yeah, I know it's hard to believe, but...

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:21.490
Things have been pretty unbelievable
all this time anyway.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:26.330
We probably won't remember about anyone.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:30.460
It's possible that we'll barely
know about ourselves.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:33.230
Hey, are you guys okay with that?

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:37.640
Becoming all alone, for ever and ever? Tell me!

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:41.710
Alone...I've been alone for a long time.

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:43.340
Claire...

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:47.320
I thought I was alone.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:50.750
And I would've never realized it unless
something like this happened.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:53.080
Yuan, and my brother...

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:59.560
I finally realize that I haven't been alone, but...

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:02.700
We're all going to be alone.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:07.200
We're going to forget about all the people
who are close to us like it's nothing.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:12.230
Leaving all the people who're
close to us behind, we will...

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:16.440
We...

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:20.080
We...

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:24.190
Oh, stop it. This is weird, isn't it?

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:27.450
Calling us "we" when we're about to be all alone.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:33.290
So, we're even going to forget
about each other, right?

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:39.800
Right, we'll all forget about
each other, together...

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:41.770
Together...

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:47.260
Seriously, this is so weird. We'll be alone,
but now we're saying "together."

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:51.010
But if you look at it that way...

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:52.550
Yeah...

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:54.650
It's just a little, but for some reason I...

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:56.980
It's time to stop chatting.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:23.480
When it's all over, I'll bring you here, Anna.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:28.380
I guess this one would be too spicy,

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:30.550
so we should ask them to go
easy on the chili peppers.

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:33.650
No, you can't have a soda.
You know what Mom told me?

00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:36.190
She said you shouldn't drink
those while you're a kid.

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:38.030
Let's get you orange juice instead!

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:41.320
You can get carbonated drinks
when you get a little older.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:58.280
Is this Neil? It's me. I saw her at Coney Island!

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:02.250
I guess, "I saw her ghost" would
be more accurate.

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:05.790
The ghost I've been dying to see...

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:08.410
What? Ghost?

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:11.190
No way!

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:14.230
We guessed it right, Neil!

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:16.300
We'd better celebrate when you get back!

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:18.400
Why did you act alone without
consulting anyone?

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.700
Where are you right now?
I'll come right away.

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:20.970
Excuse me...

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:22.870
No, she's waiting.
Excuse me...

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:23.770
No, she's waiting.

00:12:23.770 --> 00:12:26.110
No way am I going to let her pull
a disappearing act on me now.

00:12:26.110 --> 00:12:29.110
Wait a second! I'm coming too!

00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:33.710
Let's say our guess was right, but if that's the
case dealing with this alone would be too...

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:36.180
I should be the only one who gets possessed!

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:37.810
H...Hey, wait!

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:43.410
H...Hey!

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.610
I took care of them.

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:09.650
We called you, but you never showed up.

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:11.690
I know that.

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:13.810
There's something we wanted to ask you.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:19.160
Why didn't you tell us about losing memories?

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:23.300
Follow me.

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:24.920
What do we do?

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.340
Let's go.

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:29.960
All right.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:50.020
That's Lula and J.C., right?

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:52.150
About your question earlier...

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.360
I couldn't tell you.

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:56.630
That's all.

00:13:56.630 --> 00:13:59.700
You couldn't tell us? Why not?

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:05.740
Even after I found out the truth,
I still didn't want to lose him.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:09.140
I didn't want to think about what would
happen after I lost my memories.

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:12.250
I felt like I was going crazy
when I thought about it.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:18.080
So, I chose to live my life with him without
thinking about it and resolving my feelings.

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:22.690
The shock you'd experience
by finding out the truth...

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:27.360
Besides, I haven't been able to
find the answer myself,

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:29.330
so I couldn't tell you.

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:35.770
Lise!

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:47.170
Damn it! Lise!

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:54.280
Wait! I said, wait, Lise!

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:57.290
Lise!

00:14:57.860 --> 00:15:01.760
Lise! Yeah, there's no doubt! You're alive!

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:04.990
You're not a ghost! Listen, you're alive!

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:10.230
You're Lise. Am I right? Why?
What are you doing here?

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:13.410
Who brought you here?

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:18.140
What does that person look like?
Listen! Look at me!

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:24.420
Drugs...I see! I knew that pharmaceutical
company was involved!

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:26.940
Lise! Snap out of it! Up until now you've been...

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:47.340
J.C., I'm sorry. It's my fault.

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:51.280
It turned out like this, because
I was procrastinating!

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:55.050
I love you forever.

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:59.780
So even after the battle is over and I lose
my memories, that will never disappear.

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:04.150
I love you more than anybody else.

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:08.730
It's ready.

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:14.230
Wait!

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:19.100
No, please go ahead.

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:32.220
I've never seen Lula like that.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:35.960
When I lose my memories and disappear,

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:39.130
I wonder if Paul and Carrie will mourn like her?

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:42.130
I might not have anyone who'd do that for me.

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:43.760
That's not true.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:48.130
I don't need your artificial comfort
at a time like this.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:54.230
I don't really know whether they'd
mourn me either.

00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:58.980
There's a place I want to go.

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:00.280
Huh?

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.790
It's been a while since we last came here.

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:13.960
All kinds of unbelievable stuff
have happened since then

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:17.060
and we haven't even had time
to think about Lise.

00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:19.970
But we've never forgotten about her.

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:21.260
Yeah...

00:17:27.470 --> 00:17:30.940
You know Lise hates cold weather.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:34.980
Oh, yeah! Now that I think about it, she was
always carrying a light shawl with her.

00:17:34.980 --> 00:17:36.750
I remember that thing looked so grown-up!

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:40.020
You're right. She'd always order
hot drinks at the cafe.

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:42.190
She just always looked reserved.

00:17:42.190 --> 00:17:43.820
But she can't handle hot liquid.

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:50.530
Right, she seems mature,
but she can be childish sometimes.

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:53.100
It's so embarrassing to go
to the movies with her,

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:54.970
because she'll be crying next
to you during the movie!

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:59.840
That's right, she's very honest to her feelings.

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:01.780
That almost makes me jealous.

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:06.780
I see, I don't know much about
mourning and stuff,

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:11.150
but I guess the ones who're left behind would
never forget about the person who's gone.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:12.350
Yeah...

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:13.980
That's true.

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:20.190
I wonder if someone will reminisce
about me like this?

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:23.030
The guy you always hang out with,
Yuan, was that his name?

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:25.260
You sure he doesn't have a crush on you?

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:31.770
You're right, I don't think Yuan
will forget about me.

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:34.140
Look how easily you admitted that!

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:36.480
You have a lot of friends too, Rachel.

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:40.350
Well, I don't know.
Things got sour between us, so...

00:18:40.350 --> 00:18:41.920
They'll probably never forget the
arguments you've had, I bet!

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:43.710
What's that supposed to mean?

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:47.590
When the friendship goes sour,

00:18:47.590 --> 00:18:51.320
I think the ones who're left behind
regret it for a long time.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:53.260
Yeah...

00:18:53.260 --> 00:19:00.800
Even if I lose my memories, Paul and Carrie
will always remember me.

00:19:00.800 --> 00:19:03.070
Yeah, definitely.

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:06.060
Right, they won't forget you.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:13.450
I don't know what it is. You know, I've
felt like I was all alone lately, but...

00:19:14.310 --> 00:19:19.150
Yeah, they won't forget you. I think so too.

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:24.860
Then, I want to live my life right up until the
very moment I lose all my memories!

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:27.230
If my siblings will remember about me...

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:28.200
Yeah...

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:33.630
"Live your life right", huh? What would you
have to do to make it right, I wonder?

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:35.840
We can find that out as we go, starting now.

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:37.200
I'm sure.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:38.470
Yeah...

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:40.170
We have to find out.

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:44.380
It wouldn't be so cool if the only things they
remembered about us were bad!

00:19:44.380 --> 00:19:45.550
Like what?

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:46.750
Let's see...

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:48.480
If they'd remember anything about you,
you'd want it to be like,

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:50.810
"She was beautiful" or
"She had a great sense of style."

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:07.900
No wonder it's freezing.

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:10.700
Yeah...

00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:14.830
They will remember us.

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:18.870
Yeah...

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:22.720
We're not alone.

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:24.340
Right...

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:30.690
Who...Who are you?!

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:32.460
You must've done this to Lise!

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:36.030
No, not just Lise, other young girls too!

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:37.630
What are you after?

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:41.600
Tell me, what's been going on inside
that pharmaceutical company?

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:44.400
Is there any need to answer your questions?

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:45.670
What?!

00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:49.040
After all, you're about to disappear.

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:22.600
No!

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:31.390
My only love sprung from my only hate

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:33.790
Too early seen unknown, and known too late

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:38.720
Prodigious birth of love it is to me,
that I must love a loathed enemy

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:41.560
Step by step kimi to deatte

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:44.130
Toki wo wasurete odoriakashita

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:46.430
Hoshi ni yadoru sadame wo shirazu ni

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:48.970
I can't stop falling in love

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:51.540
Fujitsu na tsuki no kaketa moraru ni

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:53.870
Terasareru no wa michita desire

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:56.240
Sadame wo daita boku wa sakenda

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:58.810
"Wherefore art thou Juliet?"

00:21:58.810 --> 00:22:00.610
Oroka na koi dato

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:02.950
Azawarau ga iisa

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:05.520
Subete nagedashite

00:22:06.020 --> 00:22:07.950
Ima sugu ni yuku kara

00:22:08.620 --> 00:22:10.990
Oh, my Juliet...

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:15.430
Ne kamisama oshiete yo

00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:20.660
Dou sureba negai wa kanau

00:22:21.030 --> 00:22:25.310
Ah! Konnani setsunakute

00:22:25.310 --> 00:22:28.210
Yozora ni naku yo

00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:36.350
Ne dare mo ga konna omoi wo daite

00:22:36.350 --> 00:22:39.590
Nemuri ni tsuku no

00:22:39.590 --> 00:22:43.890
Ah! Ima sugu me wo samashite

00:22:43.890 --> 00:22:46.730
Uso dato waratte yo

00:22:46.730 --> 00:22:49.160
Oh, my sweet Juliet

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:53.270
Nemureru kimi to na mo naki boku wa

00:22:53.270 --> 00:22:54.770
Higeki no ame ni utare

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:56.430
Say good die

00:23:02.140 --> 00:23:06.750
The presence of friends, the revealed secret...

00:23:06.750 --> 00:23:09.750
On the snowy night, the girl was captured.

00:23:09.750 --> 00:23:10.720
Episode #19
Feelings That Don't Come Across
On the snowy night, the girl was captured.

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:14.520
